IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cp4-post-retirement`

-- Tests of sections 59.1 and 59.2 (post-retirement benefit and post-retirement disability benefit). Every
-- expected value is worked out by hand from the text, as written beside the assertion. Earnings, indices and
-- factors are invented.

§ `Tests -- sections 59.1 and 59.2`

§§ `Fixtures`

-- A Pension Index series, positionally 1986 to 2020: 100 for 1986 to 2018 (33 years), 102 (2019), 105 (2020).
`the test series` MEANS LIST 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 102, 105

§§ `The shape of each portion`

-- A = 12000, G = 9000, H = 10000 so F = 0.9, B = 40000, C = 0.00625, D = 50000, E = 0.9:
-- A x F / B = 12000 x 0.9 / 40000 = 0.27; x C = 0.0016875; x D = 84.375; x E = 75.9375; / 12 = 6.328125.
#ASSERT `cp4 a portion of a post-retirement benefit` 12000 9000 10000 40000 0.00625 50000 0.9 EQUALS JUST 6.328125
-- A is zero: there is nothing to count, whatever F is.
#ASSERT `cp4 a portion of a post-retirement benefit` 0 0 0 40000 0.00625 50000 0.9 EQUALS JUST 0
-- H is zero with a positive A, or B is zero: F or the ratio to B is not defined.
#ASSERT `cp4 a portion of a post-retirement benefit` 12000 9000 0 40000 0.00625 50000 0.9 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `cp4 a portion of a post-retirement benefit` 12000 9000 10000 0 0.00625 50000 0.9 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Section 59.1(1.1), (2) -- the base portion`

-- C is 0.00625: the same inputs as above.
#ASSERT `s 59.1(1.1) — the base portion of a post-retirement benefit` 12000 9000 10000 40000 50000 0.9 EQUALS JUST 6.328125
-- (2): if the earnings are earned in the year the contributory period ends, A is the greater of 0 and the amount
-- under 53(1) less the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings x months / 12: 45000 - 40000 x 4/12 = 45000 - 40000/3 = 95000/3.
#ASSERT `s 59.1(2) — the amount used for A in subsection (1.1)` TRUE 45000 40000 4 EQUALS 95000 DIVIDED BY 3
-- A smaller amount (10000) gives a negative result, so the greater of 0 and it: 0.
#ASSERT `s 59.1(2) — the amount used for A in subsection (1.1)` TRUE 10000 40000 4 EQUALS 0
-- Otherwise A is the amount under 53(1) as it stands.
#ASSERT `s 59.1(2) — the amount used for A in subsection (1.1)` FALSE 45000 40000 4 EQUALS 45000

§§ `Section 59.1(3), (4) -- the first additional portion`

-- (a) to (d): the amount for the year before is scaled by 0.15, 0.3, 0.5 and 0.75 for a benefit commencing in 2020, 2021, 2022 and 2023.
#ASSERT `s 59.1(3) — the amount A used in subsection (3) before subsection (4)` 2020 10000 EQUALS 1500
#ASSERT `s 59.1(3) — the amount A used in subsection (3) before subsection (4)` 2021 10000 EQUALS 3000
#ASSERT `s 59.1(3) — the amount A used in subsection (3) before subsection (4)` 2022 10000 EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `s 59.1(3) — the amount A used in subsection (3) before subsection (4)` 2023 10000 EQUALS 7500
-- 2024 and later: the amount for the year before, unscaled.
#ASSERT `s 59.1(3) — the amount A used in subsection (3) before subsection (4)` 2024 10000 EQUALS 10000
-- (4): the earnings are earned in the year the first additional contributory period ends: the greater of 0 and 30000 less 40000 x 3/12 = 10000: 20000.
#ASSERT `s 59.1(4) — the amount used for A in subsection (3)` TRUE 1500 30000 40000 3 EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT `s 59.1(4) — the amount used for A in subsection (3)` TRUE 1500 5000 40000 3 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 59.1(4) — the amount used for A in subsection (3)` FALSE 1500 30000 40000 3 EQUALS 1500
-- (3) with C = 0.00208: A = 12000, F = 0.9, B = 40000, D = 50000, E = 0.9: 0.27 x 0.00208 x 50000 x 0.9 / 12 = 2.106.
#ASSERT `s 59.1(3) — the first additional portion of a post-retirement benefit` 12000 9000 10000 40000 50000 0.9 EQUALS JUST 2.106

§§ `Section 59.1(5), (6) -- the second additional portion`

-- (5) with C = 0.00833: 0.27 x 0.00833 x 50000 x 0.9 / 12 = 8.43413 / 12... worked: 0.27 x 0.00833 = 0.0022491; x 50000 = 112.455; x 0.9 = 101.2095; / 12 = 8.434125.
#ASSERT `s 59.1(5) — the second additional portion of a post-retirement benefit` 12000 9000 10000 40000 50000 0.9 EQUALS JUST 8.434125
-- (6): 30000 less the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings (20000) x 6/12 = 10000: 20000.
#ASSERT `s 59.1(6) — the amount used for A in subsection (5)` TRUE 30000 20000 6 EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT `s 59.1(6) — the amount used for A in subsection (5)` TRUE 5000 20000 6 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 59.1(6) — the amount used for A in subsection (5)` FALSE 30000 20000 6 EQUALS 30000

§§ `Section 59.1(7) -- a contributor 70 or older`

-- Born 5 May 1950, 70 on 5 May 2020. On 1 January 2020 the contributor has not reached 70, so the factor for the actual age (0.9) applies;
-- on 1 January 2021 the contributor is 70 (deemed so from 1 June 2020), so the factor of a 70-year-old (1.42) applies.
#ASSERT `s 59.1(7) — the adjustment factor E` (YMD 1950 5 5) (YMD 2020 1 1) 0.9 1.42 EQUALS 0.9
#ASSERT `s 59.1(7) — the adjustment factor E` (YMD 1950 5 5) (YMD 2021 1 1) 1.3 1.42 EQUALS 1.42
-- Born 2 January 1951: 70 on 2 January 2021, deemed so from 1 February 2021: on 1 January 2021 not yet.
#ASSERT `s 59.1(7) — the adjustment factor E` (YMD 1951 1 2) (YMD 2021 1 1) 1.3 1.42 EQUALS 1.3
#ASSERT `s 59.1(7) — the adjustment factor E` (YMD 1951 1 2) (YMD 2022 1 1) 1.3 1.42 EQUALS 1.42

§§ `Section 59.1(1) -- the aggregate`

#ASSERT `s 59.1(1) — the basic monthly amount of a post-retirement benefit` (JUST 6.328125) (JUST 2.106) (JUST 8.434125) EQUALS JUST 16.868250
#ASSERT `s 59.1(1) — the basic monthly amount of a post-retirement benefit` (JUST 6) (JUST 0) (JUST 0) EQUALS JUST 6
-- If any portion is not decided, neither is the aggregate.
#ASSERT `s 59.1(1) — the basic monthly amount of a post-retirement benefit` NOTHING (JUST 2) (JUST 3) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 59.1(1) — the basic monthly amount of a post-retirement benefit` (JUST 1) NOTHING (JUST 3) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 59.1(1) — the basic monthly amount of a post-retirement benefit` (JUST 1) (JUST 2) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 59.2`

§§ `Section 59.2 -- the post-retirement disability benefit`

-- (a): 2019 is $485.20 times the Pension Index for 2019 over that for 2018 (102/100) = 494.904.
#ASSERT `s 59.2 — the basic monthly amount of a post-retirement disability benefit` 2019 `the test series` EQUALS JUST 494.904
-- (b): 2020 is the 2019 amount times 105/102 = 485.20 x 1.05 = 509.46.
#ASSERT `s 59.2 — the basic monthly amount of a post-retirement disability benefit` 2020 `the test series` EQUALS JUST 509.46
-- 2018 and earlier: no amount; 2021: the series does not reach it.
#ASSERT `s 59.2 — the basic monthly amount of a post-retirement disability benefit` 2018 `the test series` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 59.2 — the basic monthly amount of a post-retirement disability benefit` 2021 `the test series` EQUALS NOTHING
